course: dictionary
lesson: 12802
title: Elevated: higher than the rest
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Elevated means raised up higher than the ground or things around it. «The farmhouse sat on an elevated spot above the river.» The clue is above the river: the house is higher up than the land around it.
explain: The word can also mean higher than normal. «The nurse noticed an elevated temperature, so she called the doctor.» A normal temperature is not high, so elevated means above normal. Doctors also say «elevate the injured leg», which means lift it up higher.
explain: Elevated can sound grand or formal, too. «The speech used an elevated style, with long and serious words.» When you meet elevated, ask: is it about height, or about being higher than normal? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Elevated means raised up higher than the ground or things around it.
fact: «An elevated temperature» means a temperature higher than normal.
fact: «Elevate the injured leg» means lift the leg up higher, often to help with swelling.
fact: Elevated is also the past form of elevate: «The crane elevated the load onto the roof yesterday» means it lifted the load up.
fact: Some cities have an elevated railway, a train track built high above the street.
exercise: «The village sat on an elevated spot above the flooded valley.» What does elevated mean here? | *Raised higher than the land around it | Very cold and wet | Hidden under the water | Full of noise
exercise: «The nurse said the baby had an elevated temperature.» What does elevated mean? | Very short | Exactly normal | *Higher than normal | Lower than normal
exercise: Grandad says, «Elevate your sore foot on a cushion.» What should you do? | Put it in cold water and forget it | Wrap it tightly in paper | *Put your foot up higher on a cushion | Run on it to make it strong
test: «His elevated position on the hill let him see the whole town.» What does elevated mean here? | Very sad and quiet | *Higher up than the ground around it | Lost in the fog | Hidden behind a tree
test: «The speech used an elevated style, with long and grand words.» What does elevated mean here? | Hard to see | Short and quick | Silly and loud | *Grand or serious in style
exam: «The elevated railway ran above the busy street.» What does elevated mean here? | Painted bright red | Built under the ground | *Built high above the ground | Closed for repairs
